            <ArticleTitle>[Extensive pneumatization of the posterior skull].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1036-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00113-012-2318-5</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hyperpneumatization of the craniocervical bones is a very rare disorder and there are only assumptions as to the cause of this potentially dangerous condition. This article reports the case of a 44-year-old patient with severe pneumatization who became symptomatic after a minor skiing accident without any direct trauma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
